# Editorial Discipline & Content Style (High-Signal, Zero Fluff)

Travelers use this itinerary on the move. Copy must be austere, factual, and free of marketing noise.

## Concrete Facts Only

Every sentence must carry practical utility: exact times, distances, prices, opening hours, dress codes, ticket rules. Never speculate. Prefer exact instructions over vague advice.

## Zero Marketing Clichés

Ban promotional hype, superlatives, and brochure language (e.g. “magiczna atmosfera”, “zapierające dech widoki”, “perełka”). Replace with operational facts: queues, water, tickets, walking time.

## No Duplication Across Hierarchy

Never repeat the same fact in title, subtitle, badge, and body. If an element adds no new indispensable data, delete it.

## No Gratuitous Tags

Delete decorative chips with no decision value (“Kultura”, “Zabytek”, “Zwiedzanie”). Keep only operational badges (tickets bought, reservation required, free entry).

## Tone

Short, telegraphic sentences. Bold lead-ins for scanning. Bullets over narrative. Buttons state the action: “Otwórz trasę w Google Maps”, “Dzień 2”, “Szczegóły transferu”.
